  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 319 AM EDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nMonday - Friday Night\n\nAs the high pressure begins to shift east of the Ohio Valley on \nTuesday, southerly flow will return. This will lead to increasing \ntemperatures back into the mid 80s by mid week. Moisture will also \nbegin to advect back into the area rising dewpoints back into the \n60s by Thursday. \n\nA shortwave disturbance is expected to move through the Great Lakes \nregion, while a low pressure system develops over the Plains. \nFrontal boundaries associated with both systems will bring precip \nchances back into the forecast Wednesday and Thursday. Rain showers \nwill likely move through the northern half of the area as the \nnorthern disturbance moves through. Additional rain showers are \nexpected to move across the area as the second boundary pushes \nthrough. This could linger into Friday night as the low pressure \nsystem begins to eject into the northern stream.",
